module AmanaX.Investor.InvestorProfile where

-- | Step 11 (docs/prompt.md): "Investors complete onboarding." Unlike every
-- other role, an Investor is not an Organization — it's an individual, and
-- gets its own platform-managed Daml party rather than sharing a firm's
-- party the way multiple Users share one Organization's party (§3.3, and
-- the module comment on AmanaX.Identity.Organization.OrgRole). This record
-- is both the identity record (its `investor` party is freshly allocated
-- at creation, same as an Organization's `party`) and the KYC record, in
-- one template — there's no separate User-equivalent for investors since
-- there's exactly one human per investor party.
data KycStatus
  = KycPending
  | KycVerified
  | KycRejected
  deriving (Eq, Show)

-- | Signatory operator, same authorization shape as Organization/User:
-- the platform (backend, acting with the Operator's authority) admits the
-- investor onto the network by allocating its party and creating this
-- record — even though the investor self-initiates onboarding, the actual
-- ledger write is backend-driven, consistent with every other identity
-- record in this system. The chosen Distributor is an observer so it can
-- review and decide on the KYC outcome.
template InvestorProfile
  with
    operator : Party
    investor : Party
    distributor : Party
    fullName : Text
    email : Text
    kycStatus : KycStatus
  where
    signatory operator
    observer investor, distributor

    ensure fullName /= "" && email /= ""

    -- No contract key — see the same note in Organization.daml.

    choice InvestorProfile_Verify : ContractId InvestorProfile
      controller distributor
      do create this with kycStatus = KycVerified

    choice InvestorProfile_Reject : ContractId InvestorProfile
      with rejectionReason : Text
      controller distributor
      do create this with kycStatus = KycRejected
